WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:01.834
-Welcome back.

00:00:01.834 --> 00:00:03.168
It's been a while
since you've last seen us,

00:00:03.168 --> 00:00:05.338
and you're probably wondering
why I'm not in the attic.

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:07.273
Well, if you recall,
two weeks ago,

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:09.976
I entered the attic door,
not knowing where it would lead.

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:12.846
And it turns out, it was a
portal to my in-laws' house.

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:14.313
And while I love my in-laws,

00:00:14.313 --> 00:00:18.117
it is a slightly disappointing
outcome for a magic door.

00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:19.185
I mean, if the wardrobe in

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:20.519
"The Lion, the Witch,
and the Wardrobe"

00:00:20.519 --> 00:00:22.688
led to a TJ Maxx --
way different book.

00:00:22.688 --> 00:00:24.124
Way less popular.

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:26.092
With that said, there's a lot
to like about the new space,

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:27.393
because there are
only three things

00:00:27.393 --> 00:00:28.928
I ask for in a makeshift studio.

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:31.697
It has to be quiet,
has to have good Internet,

00:00:31.697 --> 00:00:34.534
and it has to not be haunted by
the ghost of an old sea captain.

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:37.503
And this baby
checks all the boxes.

00:00:37.503 --> 00:00:41.707
-Arggghh! Of that only a fool
would be certain!

00:00:41.707 --> 00:00:43.042
-Now, there are some downsides.

00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:45.077
I did not bring my beloved
copy of "The Thorn Birds"

00:00:45.077 --> 00:00:47.747
with me on the journey,
but I assure you it is safe

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:50.516
under the watchful eye
of attic protector Ethan Hawke.

00:00:50.516 --> 00:00:52.351
And he is the perfect choice
to guard "The Thorn Birds,"

00:00:52.351 --> 00:00:56.489
as Ethan Hawke is America's
greatest avian-named actor.

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:57.657
Wait. Is that right?

00:00:57.657 --> 00:00:59.692
-First one to miss
watches the winner eat.

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:01.928
-Yeah. Yeah, that's right.

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:04.197
But if I learned anything
in the portal,

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:06.299
it's to stop being so negative,
you know?

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:08.868
Celebrate the small things
in life that make us happy.

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:10.203
And I'm just [bleep] with you.

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:12.338
The US is an object
of horror and humiliation

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:14.273
across the world
as our coronavirus pandemic

00:01:14.273 --> 00:01:16.875
spins further out of control
and a desperate president

00:01:16.875 --> 00:01:19.679
tries to force students
and teachers back to school

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:21.214
without a plan
to keep them safe.

00:01:21.214 --> 00:01:23.950
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:27.854
♪♪

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:29.522
Let's just take stock
of where we are right now.

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:32.225
Four months after the first wave
of coronavirus lockdowns

00:01:32.225 --> 00:01:33.792
as countries across the world

00:01:33.792 --> 00:01:35.661
have successfully
suppressed their outbreaks

00:01:35.661 --> 00:01:37.997
and resumed
some semblance of normalcy,

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:40.700
the outbreak here in the U S
is worse than it's ever been.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.368
More than 130,000 have died.

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:43.669
The country just set a record

00:01:43.669 --> 00:01:46.005
of nearly 70,000 new cases
in one day.

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:48.741
The state of Florida
shattered the national record

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:50.977
for new daily cases
with over 15,000.

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:52.745
People are lining up for hours

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:54.714
in the scorching heat
just to get tested.

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:56.815
Frontline workers
are again facing

00:01:56.815 --> 00:01:58.617
potential shortages
of protective equipment.

00:01:58.617 --> 00:02:00.153
Patients are waiting hours

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:02.187
in ambulances
to get hospital beds.

00:02:02.187 --> 00:02:04.590
Scientists are now warning
of a potential wave

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:06.326
of COVID-related brain damage.

00:02:06.326 --> 00:02:08.494
Unemployment is still worse
than it's been

00:02:08.494 --> 00:02:10.663
since the Great Depression
as new claims keep pouring in.

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:12.031
Nearly a third of households

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:13.833
missed their
July housing payments.

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:15.167
As many as 28 million people

00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:16.603
are facing eviction
by September.

00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:18.504
Americans are banned
from traveling to Europe.

00:02:18.504 --> 00:02:22.007
And we can't even eat
Goya beans anymore.

00:02:22.007 --> 00:02:23.843
I mean,
what am I supposed to do?

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:27.580
Go back to Bush Beans?
Those beans invaded Iraq.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.448
The point is,
the country's on fire

00:02:29.448 --> 00:02:31.116
after a once-in-a-century
cataclysm

00:02:31.116 --> 00:02:33.485
that has made us a pariah state
and an object

00:02:33.485 --> 00:02:36.021
of national humiliation
to the rest of the world.

00:02:36.021 --> 00:02:38.557
And, yet, this --
this is what the President

00:02:38.557 --> 00:02:40.693
of the United States
is focused on.

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:42.128
-He hasn't taken
any cognitive tests

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:43.930
'cause he couldn't pass one.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.832
I actually took one when I --

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:48.134
very recently when, I, uh --
when I was --

00:02:48.134 --> 00:02:50.269
You know,
the radical left was saying,

00:02:50.269 --> 00:02:52.272
"Is he all there?
Is he all there?"

00:02:52.272 --> 00:02:55.575
And I proved I was all there
'cause I aced it.

00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:56.842
I aced the test.

00:02:56.842 --> 00:02:58.677
And he should take
the same exact test,

00:02:58.677 --> 00:02:59.879
a very standard test.

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:04.016
I took it at
Walter Reed Medical Center

00:03:04.016 --> 00:03:06.619
in front of doctors,
and they were very surprised.

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:08.821
They said,
"That's an unbelievable thing.

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:11.024
Rarely does anybody do
what you just did."

00:03:11.024 --> 00:03:13.325
-The test you took
is basically a placemat

00:03:13.325 --> 00:03:15.194
you give a child
at a restaurant.

00:03:15.194 --> 00:03:17.129
If you gave this
to a 10-year-old

00:03:17.129 --> 00:03:19.498
at Chuck E. Cheese,
they'd say, "Come on, man.

00:03:19.498 --> 00:03:22.001
At least give me a maze
or a jumble. Challenge me."

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:23.903
That's like going
to the optometrist

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:26.639
and bragging
that you saw the "E."

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:28.407
Also, I'm willing to bet
Trump thinks he aced it

00:03:28.407 --> 00:03:30.342
because the doctor who gave it
to him, Ronny Jackson,

00:03:30.342 --> 00:03:32.411
probably told him he aced it
even if he didn't.

00:03:32.411 --> 00:03:33.946
I mean, you guys remember?

00:03:33.946 --> 00:03:35.682
You guys remember
sweaty Ronny over here?

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:37.650
The guy who said Trump
had the weight and build

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:40.286
of a college linebacker
rather than a divorced possum?

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:43.156
Of course, any doctor
who goes by "Ronny" is suspect.

00:03:43.156 --> 00:03:45.792
Even a damn chiropractor
would call himself Dr. Ron,

00:03:45.792 --> 00:03:48.361
if only to make sure
it fit on the vanity plate.

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:50.563
I'm sure when he looked
at Trump's test,

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:53.099
he had to say, "Mr. President,
you nailed it.

00:03:53.099 --> 00:03:55.201 line:0%
That IS a dog
with a knife for a nose."

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:57.403 line:0%
Of course, if Trump
really wanted to prove

00:03:57.403 --> 00:03:59.072
his intelligence,
he could show us the results

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:01.174
of the same tests
millions of other Americans

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:02.909
take every year,
and that's the SAT,

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:04.376
but as we learned,

00:04:04.376 --> 00:04:06.378
last year he instructed
his attorney Michael Cohen

00:04:06.378 --> 00:04:09.581
to threaten his schools
to never release his SAT scores.

00:04:09.581 --> 00:04:12.484
And then last week, a tell-all
book by Trump's niece,

00:04:12.484 --> 00:04:14.453
who's also
a clinical psychologist,

00:04:14.453 --> 00:04:16.355
alleged that Trump
didn't take the SATs.

00:04:16.355 --> 00:04:18.090
He paid a friend
to take them for him.

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:19.659
Now, that claim
has been disputed,

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:22.228
but, honestly, there's
no flattering option here.

00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:25.298
Either Trump paid another kid
to take the SATs for him

00:04:25.298 --> 00:04:27.166
or he took them himself

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:29.535
and his scores were so bad,
he refused to show anyone.

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:31.136
There's no, like,
third option here

00:04:31.136 --> 00:04:32.572
where he kept his scores hidden

00:04:32.572 --> 00:04:35.108
because he was afraid people
would know they were too good.

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:36.909
Trump's not some MIT janitor

00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:39.311
solving math problems
and not telling anyone.

00:04:39.311 --> 00:04:41.814
If he was, the teacher
would come in to find "FART"

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:43.182
scrawled on the blackboard.

00:04:43.182 --> 00:04:45.251
"Did you do this?"
"It wasn't me."

00:04:45.251 --> 00:04:46.852
"You signed your name."

00:04:46.852 --> 00:04:48.354
Although I have to say, to me,

00:04:48.354 --> 00:04:50.389
the most indelible quote
from the book

00:04:50.389 --> 00:04:52.959
is Mary Trump's description
of her uncle's cognitive state.

00:04:52.959 --> 00:04:54.260
Here's what she had to say.

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:56.995
Remember, this is the most
powerful man in the world

00:04:56.995 --> 00:04:58.564
she is talking about.

00:05:11.577 --> 00:05:16.082 line:0%
But...he correctly identified
a camel on a piece of paper.

00:05:16.082 --> 00:05:19.118 line:0%
He came -- He came close.
He came close.

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:21.521
That's a relative
and a clinical psychologist

00:05:21.521 --> 00:05:24.323
saying the President's brain
is so deeply broken

00:05:24.323 --> 00:05:26.725
in so many fundamental ways

00:05:26.725 --> 00:05:28.527
that, in order to
accurately diagnose him,

00:05:28.527 --> 00:05:30.396
a team of scientists
would have to study him

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:32.898
extensively like some
sort of recently unearthed

00:05:32.898 --> 00:05:34.400
15,00-year-old Cro-Magnon man.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.635
She's talking about him
like they found him

00:05:36.635 --> 00:05:39.171
encased in a block of ice
in a loin cloth.

00:05:39.171 --> 00:05:41.307
He's "En-Senile Man."

00:05:41.307 --> 00:05:46.379
-I'm hopeful this rank punnery
will not be commonplace!

00:05:46.379 --> 00:05:48.247
-But don't worry.
If you're truly worried

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:50.049
that the President
of the United States

00:05:50.049 --> 00:05:51.951
is a mentally incontinent
sociopath,

00:05:51.951 --> 00:05:54.587
he put any questions
about his cognitive abilities

00:05:54.587 --> 00:05:58.524
to rest by brandishing this
nifty little factoid on Friday.

00:05:58.524 --> 00:05:59.959
-People don't remember,

00:05:59.959 --> 00:06:01.894
nobody ever heard of it
until I came along.

00:06:01.894 --> 00:06:03.596
Nobody remembered it
for a long time.

00:06:03.596 --> 00:06:05.897
Or they didn't use it, at least.
I use it all the time.

00:06:05.897 --> 00:06:09.101
Abraham Lincoln
was a Republican.

00:06:09.101 --> 00:06:11.503
You know, you say that, people
say, "I didn't know that."

00:06:11.503 --> 00:06:13.239
But he was a Republican.

00:06:13.239 --> 00:06:15.307
So, uh, we're doing a great job.

00:06:15.307 --> 00:06:18.678
-"Also, a lot of people
don't know Alexander Hamilton,

00:06:18.678 --> 00:06:23.816
much like his country,
was young, scrappy, and hungry.

00:06:23.816 --> 00:06:26.919
So, uh, you know,
we're doing a great job."

00:06:26.919 --> 00:06:29.054
Obviously, what he means
is he didn't know

00:06:29.054 --> 00:06:31.290
Lincoln was a Republican,
but my favorite part is when

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:35.327
he ends that dumb aside
with, "So, uh..."

00:06:35.327 --> 00:06:37.796
Even he doesn't know what point
he was trying to make.

00:06:37.796 --> 00:06:40.132
He's like a guy who's
running out of things to say

00:06:40.132 --> 00:06:41.967
and just starts reciting facts
he learned

00:06:41.967 --> 00:06:43.836
on Snapple caps
but mixes them up.

00:06:43.836 --> 00:06:46.071
"People don't know this,
but beavers, uh --

00:06:46.071 --> 00:06:48.374
beavers spend
two weeks of their life

00:06:48.374 --> 00:06:51.010
waiting at traffic lights
for lizards to do pushups.

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:55.147
So, uh...
want to take the SATs for me?"

00:06:55.147 --> 00:06:57.016
That's the guy overseeing
the worst response

00:06:57.016 --> 00:06:59.118
to the coronavirus pandemic
anywhere in the world.

00:06:59.118 --> 00:07:01.019
Just for some perspective,
on July 1st,

00:07:01.019 --> 00:07:04.424
the state of Arizona alone
recorded more cases in one day

00:07:04.424 --> 00:07:05.991
than the entirety
of the European Union.

00:07:05.991 --> 00:07:07.726
Yesterday, according
to "The New York Times,"

00:07:07.726 --> 00:07:12.231
Germany reported 159 new cases,
Canada reported 243 new cases,

00:07:12.231 --> 00:07:16.669
while the US reported
a total of 57,789 new cases.

00:07:16.669 --> 00:07:18.670
So, you know, perfect timing
for the President

00:07:18.670 --> 00:07:20.272
to start wearing a mask.

00:07:20.272 --> 00:07:21.974
Of course, he went with black.

00:07:21.974 --> 00:07:23.975
It looks like there's
about to be a shootout

00:07:23.975 --> 00:07:25.644
at the Golden Corral.

00:07:25.644 --> 00:07:29.081
-Arggh! I will admit
that one tickled me!

00:07:29.081 --> 00:07:30.849
-Seriously, dude,
get a different mask.

00:07:30.849 --> 00:07:32.451
That color
combined with your mane

00:07:32.451 --> 00:07:34.053
makes you look like
a muzzled horse.

00:07:34.053 --> 00:07:36.688
Trump's team acted like this
was a big deal, but who cares?

00:07:36.688 --> 00:07:38.157
You're four months late.

00:07:38.157 --> 00:07:40.593
It's like someone saying,
"Should we not do

00:07:40.593 --> 00:07:43.462
a live-action 'Cats'?" now.

00:07:43.462 --> 00:07:45.497
It took Trump just as long
to learn that masks work

00:07:45.497 --> 00:07:47.700
as it did for him to learn
that Lincoln was a Republican.

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:49.234
The rest of the world
is watching us

00:07:49.234 --> 00:07:50.736
with pity and horror.

00:07:50.736 --> 00:07:53.539
European countries are getting
back to some version of normal

00:07:53.539 --> 00:07:55.141
while keeping
their economies intact.

00:07:55.141 --> 00:07:57.943
In June, New Zealand lifted
all of its COVID restrictions

00:07:57.943 --> 00:07:59.711
after declaring the country
virus-free.

00:07:59.711 --> 00:08:02.047
Vietnam, a country
of nearly 100 million,

00:08:02.047 --> 00:08:03.983
which shares a border
with China,

00:08:03.983 --> 00:08:06.318
hasn't seen a domestically
transmitted infection

00:08:06.318 --> 00:08:09.121
in nearly three months
and has recorded zero deaths.

00:08:09.121 --> 00:08:11.090
And Japan just reopened concerts
and sporting events

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:13.659
to spectators, which is good
news, because, until recently,

00:08:13.659 --> 00:08:15.361
at least one of
their baseball teams

00:08:15.361 --> 00:08:19.297
was forced to fill the stands
with robot fans.

00:08:19.297 --> 00:08:21.833
Those robots may look adorable,
but I assure you,

00:08:21.833 --> 00:08:24.770
the adorable ones are
the first ones to turn on you

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:26.571
when the robot wars start.

00:08:26.571 --> 00:08:29.809
Going to be a hell of a thing
when that's the last face

00:08:29.809 --> 00:08:31.477
you see choking the life
out of you.

00:08:31.477 --> 00:08:32.945
"Why?"

00:08:32.945 --> 00:08:35.414
[Robotic voice] "Why did you
make me go to a baseball game?"

00:08:35.414 --> 00:08:38.150
And many countries have also
reopened their schools

00:08:38.150 --> 00:08:40.352
thanks to the success
in suppressing the virus.

00:08:40.352 --> 00:08:42.255
Meanwhile, here in the US,
the President

00:08:42.255 --> 00:08:44.022
wants to force
teachers and students

00:08:44.022 --> 00:08:46.758
back into classrooms
as the outbreak worsens,

00:08:46.758 --> 00:08:49.161
without sufficient health
and safety protocols in place

00:08:49.161 --> 00:08:51.230
because he thinks
it'll help the economy

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:53.032
and, thus, his re-election.

00:08:53.032 --> 00:08:57.336
-We have to open our schools.
Open our schools.

00:08:57.336 --> 00:09:00.105
[ Applause ]
Stop this nonsense.

00:09:00.105 --> 00:09:02.407
We open our schools.

00:09:02.407 --> 00:09:06.712
Germany, Norway,
so many countries right now,

00:09:06.712 --> 00:09:08.781
they're open,
the schools are open.

00:09:08.781 --> 00:09:10.349
And they're doing just fine.

00:09:10.349 --> 00:09:12.918
-Yeah, that's because
they suppressed their outbreaks,

00:09:12.918 --> 00:09:14.620
you sadistic sack of laundry.

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:16.722
You rushed everyone back to work
too soon against the advice

00:09:16.722 --> 00:09:18.424
of your own scientists
just to please the Dow,

00:09:18.424 --> 00:09:20.559
and now we have 60,000
new cases every day

00:09:20.559 --> 00:09:22.227
and we're banned
from traveling to Europe.

00:09:22.227 --> 00:09:24.931
Do you know what that means?
If Americans can't go to Europe,

00:09:24.931 --> 00:09:27.699
who is going to wear shorts
and Mickey ears to the Louvre?

00:09:27.699 --> 00:09:29.535
And, look, everyone
wants schools to reopen.

00:09:29.535 --> 00:09:31.136
Believe me,
I desperately want my kids

00:09:31.136 --> 00:09:32.604
to go back to school
in the fall.

00:09:32.604 --> 00:09:34.240
I mean, to keep them busy
during this,

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:35.674
I've had to put them
on the show,

00:09:35.674 --> 00:09:38.176
and now they're demanding to
know when their next gig is.

00:09:38.176 --> 00:09:39.745
They have agents now.

00:09:39.745 --> 00:09:41.447
I walked by the little one's
room the other day

00:09:41.447 --> 00:09:44.316
and heard him on the phone
demanding "points on the gross."

00:09:44.316 --> 00:09:47.353
I don't think I get
points on the gross.

00:09:47.353 --> 00:09:49.589
We might not have a giant gross.

00:09:49.589 --> 00:09:51.656
I'm talking to
a different toy boat.

00:09:51.656 --> 00:09:53.693
But Donald Trump
is the last person

00:09:53.693 --> 00:09:55.727
I would trust
with my kids' safety.

00:09:55.727 --> 00:09:57.429
He can't even be trusted
with Don Jr.'s --

00:09:57.429 --> 00:09:59.165
By the way,
my father-in-law would be like,

00:09:59.165 --> 00:10:00.666
"They're not toys.
They're antiques."

00:10:00.666 --> 00:10:02.501
He can't even be trusted
with Don Jr.'s safety.

00:10:02.501 --> 00:10:04.537
He let his oldest son
wander around the woods

00:10:04.537 --> 00:10:06.905
until he eventually decided
to become one with the stumps.

00:10:06.905 --> 00:10:08.874
Of course, eventually
the stumps made him leave

00:10:08.874 --> 00:10:11.310
because he was too boring.

00:10:11.310 --> 00:10:13.612
We just can't decouple schools
from the communities they're in.

00:10:13.612 --> 00:10:15.014
If there are outbreaks
everywhere,

00:10:15.014 --> 00:10:17.282
then schools are
going to have outbreaks, too.

00:10:17.282 --> 00:10:18.784
Even in the best of times,

00:10:18.784 --> 00:10:20.986
schools are a breeding ground
for viruses.

00:10:20.986 --> 00:10:22.988
An elementary school
is like you took

00:10:22.988 --> 00:10:24.657
a Five Points tenement building

00:10:24.657 --> 00:10:27.226
and put it on the lido deck
of a cruise ship.

00:10:27.226 --> 00:10:29.561
Every parent knows
if you have a child in school,

00:10:29.561 --> 00:10:32.164
you basically have to put
DayQuil in your coffee

00:10:32.164 --> 00:10:33.832
until they leave for college.

00:10:33.832 --> 00:10:36.067
And if you're going to force
students and teachers to go back

00:10:36.067 --> 00:10:38.370
amid a deadly pandemic,
you should at least --

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:40.072
at the very least,
have an idea

00:10:40.072 --> 00:10:41.506
for how you're
going to protect them.

00:10:41.506 --> 00:10:43.675
Instead, Education Secretary
Betsy DeVos

00:10:43.675 --> 00:10:45.677
says it's up to you
to figure out

00:10:45.677 --> 00:10:47.980
how you're going to
keep your kids safe.

00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:50.215
And if you don't, they're
going to unilaterally strip

00:10:50.215 --> 00:10:51.750
funding from your school,

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:53.485
which they don't even
have the power to do anyway.

00:10:53.485 --> 00:10:56.421
-The US hit a record number
of new cases on Friday.

00:10:56.421 --> 00:10:59.224
The number of new cases per day
is higher now

00:10:59.224 --> 00:11:03.229
in 45 of the 50 states than
when schools shut down in March.

00:11:03.229 --> 00:11:06.264
Hospitalizations are climbing
in several states,

00:11:06.264 --> 00:11:09.969
and some ICUs
are at or near capacity.

00:11:09.969 --> 00:11:12.004
So, yes or no --

00:11:12.004 --> 00:11:15.040
can you assure
students, teachers, parents

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:16.909
that they will not get
coronavirus

00:11:16.909 --> 00:11:18.978
because they're
going back to school?

00:11:21.046 --> 00:11:23.949
-Well, the key is that kids
have to get back to school.

00:11:23.949 --> 00:11:28.019
-You are compelling schools
to reopen

00:11:28.019 --> 00:11:31.389
regardless of what's happening.

00:11:31.389 --> 00:11:34.559
-No, what we're saying is that
kids need to be back in school.

00:11:34.559 --> 00:11:37.629
-Why do you not have guidance
on what a school should do

00:11:37.629 --> 00:11:40.599
just weeks before you want
those schools to reopen?

00:11:40.599 --> 00:11:44.402
And what happens
if it faces an outbreak?

00:11:44.402 --> 00:11:46.238
-You know,
there is really good examples

00:11:46.238 --> 00:11:51.410
that have been utilized in the
private sector and elsewhere,

00:11:51.410 --> 00:11:53.478
also with frontline workers
and hospitals.

00:11:53.478 --> 00:11:55.381
-You can't even get
protective equipment

00:11:55.381 --> 00:11:56.615
for doctors and nurses,

00:11:56.615 --> 00:11:58.917
but you want schools
to operate like hospitals?

00:11:58.917 --> 00:12:00.886
Why not go even further
and say schools

00:12:00.886 --> 00:12:02.254
should operate like astronauts?

00:12:02.254 --> 00:12:06.058
"There's really good examples
that have been utilized

00:12:06.058 --> 00:12:07.559
on the International
Space Station.

00:12:07.559 --> 00:12:09.695
If we launch all of our schools
into orbit,

00:12:09.695 --> 00:12:11.430
then they can't get
coronavirus."

00:12:11.430 --> 00:12:14.333
And, yet, that somehow
was not the dumbest remark

00:12:14.333 --> 00:12:15.667
a Republican politician made

00:12:15.667 --> 00:12:17.202
about re-opening schools
last week.

00:12:17.202 --> 00:12:18.670
Florida governor Ron DeSantis,

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:21.273
who has overseen
an exploding pandemic

00:12:21.273 --> 00:12:23.608
setting new records
in his state every day,

00:12:23.608 --> 00:12:26.979
said we should treat schools
like hardware stores.

00:12:26.979 --> 00:12:30.850
-If you can do Home Depot,
if you can do Walmart,

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:32.384
if you can do these things,

00:12:32.384 --> 00:12:34.219
we absolutely
can do the schools.

00:12:34.219 --> 00:12:35.620
-Yeah, man. Totally.

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:37.355
Last time I went to Home Depot,
they put me in

00:12:37.355 --> 00:12:38.557
Remedial Weather Proofing

00:12:38.557 --> 00:12:40.158
with 40 other customers
for eight hours,

00:12:40.158 --> 00:12:42.828
and halfway through we took
a break to play kickball.

00:12:42.828 --> 00:12:45.564
And if you're expecting DeSantis
to have second thoughts,

00:12:45.564 --> 00:12:47.032
don't hold your breath.

00:12:47.032 --> 00:12:50.069
Back in May, he had this to say
about those in the media

00:12:50.069 --> 00:12:52.304
who criticized
Florida's re-opening.

00:12:52.304 --> 00:12:54.639
-You've got a lot of people
in your profession

00:12:54.639 --> 00:12:57.476
who waxed poetically
for weeks and weeks

00:12:57.476 --> 00:13:00.045
about how Florida was
going to be just like New York.

00:13:00.045 --> 00:13:02.180
"Wait two weeks.
Florida's going to be next.

00:13:02.180 --> 00:13:03.848
Just like Italy.
Wait two weeks."

00:13:03.848 --> 00:13:05.984
Well, hell, we're eight weeks
away from that!

00:13:05.984 --> 00:13:07.386
And it hasn't happened!

00:13:07.386 --> 00:13:10.589
-My first question is,
how come Ron DeSantis

00:13:10.589 --> 00:13:12.624
gets his own Japanese robot?

00:13:12.624 --> 00:13:15.127
And, second, why is anyone
taking a victory lap

00:13:15.127 --> 00:13:16.529
in the middle of a pandemic?

00:13:16.529 --> 00:13:18.797
No one knows how this ends.

00:13:18.797 --> 00:13:21.000
The best most of us can do
is mitigate risk

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:23.769
for the benefit of ourselves
and others around us

00:13:23.769 --> 00:13:25.270
and take steps to make sure

00:13:25.270 --> 00:13:27.239
we're ready
for all contingencies.

00:13:27.239 --> 00:13:30.308
You can't only have a Plan A,

00:13:30.308 --> 00:13:31.777
especially when
the guy in charge

00:13:31.777 --> 00:13:33.846 line:0%
thinks "Plan A"
is how you spell "plane."

00:13:33.846 --> 00:13:37.015 line:0%
"Close enough, Mr. President!"
"Thank you, Dr. Ronny!"

00:13:37.015 --> 00:13:39.184
When you're talking about
